  "experiment": "C01",
  "title": "Industry-neutral allocations",
  "description": "This experiment asks whether industry bets account for part of the Markowitz portfolio's performance. It optimizes stock weights subject to the long and short weights summing to zero within each represented Fama\u2013French 12 industry. For example, a +5% weight in one industry's stocks must be offset by \u22125% in other stocks from that same industry. A separate portfolio requires only zero total net weight, so the comparison isolates the added industry constraints. Both original Ridge and XGBoost forecasts are tested, with the original covariance and estimated 10% annual risk scaling unchanged. Industry neutrality does not imply market-beta neutrality.",
